# Service Layer Conventions

> **Migration note:** The error handling section describes the target state. 11 existing services use `error()` from `@sveltejs/kit` directly. When writing NEW services, use the error utilities. When touching existing services, migrate toward them.

All backend business logic lives in `src/lib/server/services/<domain>.ts`.

## File Structure

- One file per domain: `teams.ts`, `matches.ts`, `payments.ts`, etc.
- Use **named exports only** — no `export default`.
- Import Prisma from `$lib/server/db` (never instantiate a new client).
- Import Prisma types from `$prisma/client.js`.

## Error Handling in Services

Services should throw errors using the utilities from `$lib/server/utils/errors`:

```typescript
import { notFound, forbidden, badRequest } from '$lib/server/utils/errors';

// ✅ CORRECT — use error utilities
export async function getTeam(id: number) {
  const team = await prisma.team.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  if (!team) notFound('Team not found');
  return team;
}

// ❌ AVOID — importing error() from @sveltejs/kit in services
import { error } from '@sveltejs/kit';
throw error(404, 'Team not found');
```

The error utilities (`notFound`, `forbidden`, `badRequest`, `conflict`, `unauthorized`) wrap SvelteKit's `error()` but keep the service layer's vocabulary clean.

## Cross-Service Calls

Services MAY import and call other services. This is expected for domain coordination (e.g., match service calling notification service). Avoid circular dependencies.

## Constants

Magic numbers for database IDs belong in `$lib/server/constants/`:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { FORMAT_1V1, FORMAT_2V2 } from '$lib/server/constants/formats';

// ❌ WRONG — magic numbers
where: { formatId: 1 }
```

## Load Function Data Mapping

Route `load` functions must NOT return raw Prisma objects. Map them to plain serializable shapes:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — explicit shape
return {
  team: {
    id: team.id,
    name: team.name,
    division: team.division?.name,
  },
};

// ❌ WRONG — leaks Prisma internals and relations
return { team };
```
